// Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded base-10 logarithm of F64
//
// The fast path is log's (log.tess) with its own tables, followed by a
// double-double product with 1/log(10). When that can't decide the rounding,
// log x comes from log's accurate dint path and is multiplied by 1/log(10) in
// dint arithmetic. Round to nearest only: log10(+-0) is -inf, a negative input
// gives NaN, NaN comes back quiet, and log10(10^n) is exactly n.
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/log10/log10.c and its dint.h via
// RazorForge's B64Log10.rf.
// log10.c: Copyright (c) 2022-2025 INRIA and CERN. Authors: Paul Zimmermann and Tom Hubrecht.
// dint.h: Copyright (c) 2022 CERN. Author: Tom Hubrecht.
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

/// Reciprocals r[i] of the fast path, 362 <= i <= 724, as F64 bits: a 10-bit approximation of 1/y for
/// i 2^-9 <= y < (i + 1) 2^-9 such that r[i] y - 1 is exact.
